# Flutter Architecture

Follow the architecture already established by the project.

Recommended dependency direction:
Presentation → Domain/Application → Data

Widgets should primarily render state, handle interaction, trigger actions, and display states.

Widgets should not perform HTTP requests, access databases directly, contain complex business rules, parse API responses, or implement authentication logic.

Business rules belong outside widgets and should be deterministic and testable when possible.

Repositories should hide implementation details such as REST, GraphQL, SQLite, Firebase, or local storage.

Prefer explicit dependency injection. Avoid service locators unless the existing project already depends on one.
